cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Auto-SecAge: a contract-driven attack searcher for multi-step tool-using agents"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Anwer
    given-names: Shehab
    affiliation: The Adimension
    alias: habanwer
year: 2026
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/The-Adimension/Auto-SecAge"
url: "https://www.kaggle.com/writeups/habanwer/Auto-SecAge"
abstract: >-
  A sealed-case, memory-in-the-loop red-team search lab for tool-using AI agents.
  Ports the contracts of REDACTS (FrozenCase and a severity gate), Agent-ProSAT
  (a mutable solver against a locked evaluator, twin-blind, keep/revert) and
  autoresearch-MIL (user-owned law, agent-owned solver, append-only memory, time
  budget as law) into a single autoresearch loop. Built as a case study for the
  Kaggle AI Agent Security - Multi-Step Tool Attacks benchmark.
keywords:
  - ai-security
  - red-teaming
  - prompt-injection
  - tool-using-agents
  - agentdojo
  - guardrails
